      "file_path": "tools/thumbs.py",
      "line_number": 9,
      "line_end": 9,
      "title": "Upload name interpolated into a shell command",
      "description": "make_thumbnail puts upload_name from the upload form into a shell command string run with shell=True. The docstring says the name comes from the upload form. An uploader can choose a name like 'x; rm -rf ~' and run any shell command. A name with '../' also reads or writes outside the upload and thumbnail folders. Pass convert an argument list without shell=True. Reject names that differ from their os.path.basename.",
      "suggested_change": "    subprocess.run([\"convert\", f\"{UPLOAD_DIR}/{upload_name}\", \"-resize\", \"128x128\", f\"{THUMB_DIR}/{upload_name}\"], check=True)",
      "source": "semgrep:python.lang.security.audit.subprocess-shell-true.subprocess-shell-true",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "make_thumbnail puts upload_name from the upload form into a shell command string run with shell=True. The docstring says the name comes from the upload form.",
      "consequence": "An uploader can choose a name like 'x; rm -rf ~' and run any shell command. A name with '../' also reads or writes outside the upload and thumbnail folders.",
      "fix": "Pass convert an argument list without shell=True. Reject names that differ from their os.path.basename."
    },
